==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ring Girl Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Pizza Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Weightlifter is a very good offensive unit against Dark enemies. It has a relatively fast attack rate, moderate recharge and cost, while its massive damage ability to Darks rips them to shreds by exploiting their low range. It is extraordinary in levels like [[Dark Premonition]], where large amounts of Dark threats spawn.

Since this unit is slow, a little expensive and doesn't have the best recharge, it's best to make the most of each.

==='''True Form'''===
Pizza Cat is an excellent [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark Cat]] overall, being one of the best non uber options. Dealing 62,900 damage to Dark enemies at Level 30 with 100% Void Fruit, Pizza Cat can steamroll many melee Darks with terrifying ease (although it can still fall back on his high HP). He also gets much better survivability in TF due to his increased HP, standing range and knockback count.

==='''Talents'''===
With [[talents]], his performance as both an anti-Dark attacker and a general midranger become better, as he gets both attack buffs (Increasing his base damage to 18,870) and a chance to create waves. His wave attacks (30% chance for a level 2 [[Wave Attack]]) not only let him deal much better damage to more durable Dark enemies (assuming it and his main attack both connect), such as [[Dark Otter]], but also allow him to snipe backliners such as [[Tackey]], [[Le'noir]] and even [[Director Kurosawah]], as long as there's a frontline present. Pizza Cat's Wave talent is considered one of the most potent talents in the game, although it is more expensive to level than [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]]'s Extra Money and Speed. [[Slow|Slow]] is a simple role compression, and can serve as an additional wall of defense against Razorback (or other Dark enemies) should options like [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] and [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] not cut it. However, with how effective said options are, this Talent is just shy of being superfluous, but it doesn't hurt to own in most instances. Finally, the Cost Down talent is mostly just for convenience as Pizza is not too expensive for what he does, but can be useful sometimes. If you choose to invest into Cost Down, leave it at level 5, so Pizza Cat would still be usable for 1200c+ restriction stages, similar to [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]]. The least valuable talent is Health Up, as Pizza rarely needs it, due to relying on outranging threats most of the time and its very high cost for how little it does.

==='''Orb'''===
Pizza obviously benefits most from a Dark Massive Damage Up Orb, which bumps up the multiplier from 4x (assuming all Void Fruit Treasures are maxed) to 4.5x. A Dark Attack Up Orb in comparison yields little benefit, since the added damage is not subject to the Massive Damage ability.

